WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.400
<i>Minds afflicted by stress 
or obsession are sometimes</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>Mysterious</b>

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.680
<i>afflicted by something "mysterious" 
and develop a "mysterious disease."</i>

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>Mysterious Disease</b>

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.260
<i>The "mysterious" cannot be 
seen by ordinary people.</i>

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:19.210
<i>However, as long as there are people in 
this world and those people have hearts,</i>

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.110
<i>there will be those who suffer 
from bizarre diseases.</i>

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:32.060
<i>And where there are mysterious diseases, 
there are also those who cure them.</i>

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:38.930
<i>Doctors who expose the secret causes hidden 
in people's sick hearts and save them.</i>

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.430
<b>Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.960
<i>"Mysterious disease specialists."</i>

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.640
Ouch.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.240
<b>Yamaguchi Ophthalmological Clinic</b>

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.240
Mayonnaise? From your eyes?

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.240
Yes. Mayonnaise is coming out of my eyes.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.650
It's a problem.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.260
You know, it's not good to 
tease adults like that.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:16.260
<b>Yamaguchi Ophthalmological Clinic</b>

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.640
It's true. Please fix it!

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.230
My mom... It's causing problems for my mom.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:20.250
Okay, okay.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.950
Bring your mom with you next time.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.870
Why won't you believe me?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.020
Excuse me.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.380
Would you like me to 
introduce you to a doctor?

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.720
He specializes in that type of disease.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:13.330
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.800
<b>Episode 1 "Condiment Tears"</b>

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.720
<b>Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.990
Kuro, did you kidnap that girl?

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.060
I mean, what else could explain it?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.730
He's a doctor?

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.430
It's all right.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.990
Everyone's put off by him at first,

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.440
but he's a great doctor.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.560
Oh, come on. Who's putting
people off, Mr. Kidnapper?

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.450
So, you have mayonnaise 
coming out of your eyes?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.850
Yes, but none of the 
hospitals will believe me.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.320
Well, mysterious diseases are 
still considered occult.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.650
Mysterious diseases?

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.650
You're more likely to catch 
a cold when you're tired.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.150
When your body is weakened, you're more 
likely to fall ill due to viruses and bacteria.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.440
Mysterious diseases work the same way.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.900
When your heart is weakened, something 
mysterious enters your body and causes mischief.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.510
Mischief?

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.420
Well, no need to worry.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.100
I'm a doctor who cures those.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.670
Mysterious Disease Specialist Dr. Ramune!

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.430
For now,

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:44.680
<b>Mother and Daughter's 10 Days</b>

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.610
we need to put on a sad movie

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:44.680
so I can see just how much
mayonnaise comes out of your eyes.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:45.720
What?

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.880
<i>Mom, don't leave me.</i>

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.730
<i>Mom!</i>

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.850
Doctor, what are you crying for?

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.290
I'm <i>not</i> crying!

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:03.660
Anyway, this child actress
named Koto is great at crying.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.920
Th-Thank you.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.530
<b>Everything is ever changing</b>

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.290
<i>Mom!</i>

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.660
What?!

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:17.450
You?! But you're nothing like her!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.910
I was acting in the movie.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.420
Acting?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.790
In that case, can you cry on
 command? Right now?

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.520
Yeah, I can.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:44.430
Ow.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:45.770
Are you okay?

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:50.670
Soy sauce.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.850
Kuro, rinse her eyes immediately.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:54.620
Right.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.510
Sorry. That must've hurt.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.010
Anyway, you can produce stuff 
that isn't mayonnaise?

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.170
Yeah.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:13.530
I've also cried ketchup, sauce, 
ponzu, and noodle soup base.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.690
They're all condiments.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.300
Then when do you cry normal tears?

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.730
Normal?

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.730
I don't know.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:30.800
My mom tells me not to cry 
even if I'm lonely or sad.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.250
She says, "Save those tears 
for when you're acting."

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:40.260
Then I forgot how to cry for real.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.110
Here's your medicine.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.340
Goldfish?

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.170
They're teabags.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.320
Put them in this teapot and drink it.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:56.480
You'll gradually stop producing condiments.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.970
And use these when you really need them.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.230
They're contact lenses.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.490
They'll stop the condiments 
while you're wearing them.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:10.800
These come with strong side effects, 
so don't use them too much.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.810
Take care.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:21.760
There's clearly an issue with
 her home environment.

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:23.180
Yeah.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.170
It's probably the cause of her tears.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.360
I'm home, Mom.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:42.640
How did things go at the hospital?

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.570
I need you to get better soon.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:48.860
You can't keep taking time off forever.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.070
I left you a boxed lunch on the table.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.200
Eat it when you're hungry.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.200
<b>Salmon Boxed Lunch</b>

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.200
<b>Half Off Discount</b>

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:07.540
<i>It's supposed to be medicine,
but it tastes like ordinary tea.</i>

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.920
Thanks for the food.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.960
Koto, congratulations on 
passing the audition!

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.120
We're having hot pot to celebrate today.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.020
Koto, I'm busy.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.830
Are boxed lunches okay for dinner?

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:28.540
Yeah!

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.910
You're asking about Koto's schedule?

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.310
She's... available that day.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.110
Anyway, her fee is...

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:42.860
I wish I could quit working.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:43.920
What?

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.980
Koto, what do you think you're saying?

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:48.600
What?

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:52.330
You were joking when you said 
you wanted to quit, right?

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:57.900
It's true. I don't want to work anymore.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.900
What was that?

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:05.460
What are you talking about?!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.230
You need to become even more famous!

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:13.840
While you're on hiatus, other new child 
actors are rising to the top!

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.360
That's not what I want.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.900
Koto?! Wait!

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:28.800
I see. So that's how it is.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:33.870
Are you using spy cams to peep 
on people's private lives again?

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.700
It's not a spy cam.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.490
It's called "Shoji Vision."

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:42.280
It allows you to use one shoji to see 
what's visible around another, right?

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.160
I'll man the sukiyaki.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.680
No! I'll do it!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:50.670
Sugar.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.120
Soy sauce.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.950
Condiments can be sweet or 
spicy, kind of like emotions.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.130
Suppressing your emotions causes stress.

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:07.360
She has to fake her own 
emotions while acting,

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.110
so instead of expressing the 
emotions she's suppressing,

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.250
the condiments are expressing them for her.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:18.350
Will that goldfish tea cure her?

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:20.180
Huh? Goldfish?

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.680
Oh, that. Pretty tasteful, right?

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.170
I bought them online.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.180
What? Online?

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.030
The tea doesn't matter.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:30.190
What's important is the teapot.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.740
The Teapot of Loose Lips.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:37.730
Drink something poured from that, and 
you'll only be able to speak the truth.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.830
You resorted to drastic treatment again?

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:44.450
What if she notices and 
stops drinking from it?

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.940
It's her choice.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.960
<b>Greenroom A</b>

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.960
<b>Kashiwagi Koto-sama</b>

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:52.020
She has to choose for herself.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.500
<i>I stopped crying condiments,</i>

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.640
<i>but when I drink that medicine,
 I can't stop myself from speaking.</i>

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.800
<i>But if I don't drink it, 
I'll cry condiments again.</i>

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.840
<i>Plus, I've got work now.</i>

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.730
Koto, why do you keep saying 
things to upset me these days?

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.520
Koto, is that good?

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.640
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:23.080
<i>What I want is selfish.</i>

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:42.520
These come with strong side effects, 
so don't use them too much.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.450
Koto, you're late!

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:53.720
Hurry up and get on standby!

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:56.640
I'm sorry.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.550
Koto-chan, are you done taking a break?

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:02.480
It's fine.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.410
I'm fine now.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.230
Hey, Kuro.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.970
<b>Joy</b>

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.010
Joy.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.510
<b>Anger</b>

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:23.500
Anger.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:25.010
<b>Grief</b>

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:24.790
Grief.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.180
Pleasure.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.510
<b>Pleasure</b>

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.720
Ow...

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.540
Have you lost your mind, Doctor?

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:33.690
No!

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:36.890
They say joy, anger, grief, and pleasure 
are the basic human emotions.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:39.680
I thought I'd try expressing a few.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.160
I see.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.540
But your face is overly expressive.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:45.770
Don't overdo it.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:47.430
How rude!

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.480
Why don't you try it?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.290
<b>Joy</b>

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:52.390
Joy.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.290
<b>Anger</b>

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:54.500
Anger

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.290
<b>Grief</b>

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:56.340
Grief.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.290
<b>Pleasure</b>

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.310
Pleasure.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.600
They're all exactly the same!

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:02.920
How rude.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.290
Keep working.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.600
Kuro, you jerk.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.770
<i>Charge! Celebrity Home Visit!</i>

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:23.900
Today we're visiting the home of number one 
tear-jerking child actor Kashiwagi Koto-chan.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.320
<i>I'm tired.</i>

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:30.540
<i>My body feels heavy.</i>

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.280
Wow!

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.440
Do all of these belong to your mother?

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:39.780
Yes.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.800
What a huge diamond.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.750
Koto-chan, do you hope to have 
stuff like this someday?

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:49.110
Koto!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.640
You're working. Pull yourself together!

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:55.430
I'm sorry.

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:04.850
Do you have any goals for 
the future, Koto-chan?

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:09.710
Well, she'd like to broaden her acting range 
and make great progress as an actress

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:12.700
instead of ending her 
career as a child actor.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:21.570
As someone trying to become 
a major actress, Koto-chan,

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:25.200
could you show us your 
specialty and cry for us?

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.220
Um, Koto-chan?

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.600
Koto, enough. You've been misbehaving.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.100
Now cry.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.190
This is your job!

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:39.190
Hurry up!

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.210
Koto-chan?!

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.380
Koto? What's wrong, Koto?

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:54.960
I-I'll call an ambulance!

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.940
I told you not to use them too much.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.760
Why did you make that choice?

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.870
Doctor?

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:07.390
Hup.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:09.430
Wh-Who are you?!

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:10.840
Her doctor.

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:13.680
Hey, you can't come in through the window.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.090
I'm using your front door.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:16.200
What?

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:18.850
Who are you boys?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:21.210
Doctor, what is this?

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.850
The side effects of the contact lenses.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:30.230
They're like a lid that temporarily 
stops the condiments from coming out.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:35.810
While the lid is closed, the condiments 
build up inside her body.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:41.410
Instead of expressing her emotions or 
releasing condiments in their place,

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:43.880
she chose to keep the lid on.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:48.310
Doctor, we don't have time 
to take things slow.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:52.380
From the looks of it, there's a considerable 
amount of condiments built up inside her body.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.810
I don't want that.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:16:00.900
When I say how I really 
feel, it causes trouble.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.640
Trouble?

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.150
You collapsing on the floor 
is way more trouble.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:09.180
What? What are you talking about, Doctor?

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:13.390
Nobody lives their whole life 
without troubling others.

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:16.670
Even I cause trouble for this guy sometimes.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.530
<i>So he </i>is<i> aware of it.</i>

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.670
If you're going to cause trouble either way, 
when it comes to expressing your emotions,

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:25.760
choose the trouble you prefer.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:28.030
I see.

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:33.120
In that case, I'd like to eat 
your cooking again, Mom.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.110
You're a doctor, aren't you?

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:39.300
Do something, will you?

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.630
A significant amount of condiments 
has built up inside Koto's body.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.060
She's on the brink of necrosis.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:50.180
In order to reduce the harm done to 
her body and release the condiments,

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:52.990
we'll need a receptacle for them.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.450
You'll be paying for that.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:57.500
And what on earth does that mean?!

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:00.150
Condiments? You're not making any sense.

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:02.570
I bet you're a quack who will demand 
a huge amount of money!

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.240
Money?

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:07.580
What are you weighing that money against?

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:13.330
Fine! I'll pay whatever 
you want! Just fix Koto!

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.950
Great news, Koto.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.130
We've got a receptacle.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.890
<i>I want to play.</i>

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.140
<i>Acting makes me tired.</i>

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:31.890
<i>I don't want to work.</i>

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:33.900
Wh-What is this?!

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:35.460
<i>I wish I could turn back time.</i>

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:38.440
<i>I want to eat Mom's cooking.</i>

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:41.650
N-No. What is this?!

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:40.620
<i>I want to play.</i>

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.860
<i>Acting makes me tired.</i>

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.930
<i>I don't want to work.</i>

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.200
<i>I want to eat Mom's cooking.</i>

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.280
<i>I don't want to work.</i>

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:48.100
<i>I want to eat Mom's cooking.</i>

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:15.390
You're kidding. You're kidding, right?

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:22.910
My clothes. My bags. My diamonds!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:27.750
The receptacle was everything you've acquired 
by sacrificing Koto's feelings.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.710
Lucky you.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.400
Normally, Koto would've ended up like that.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.210
I'm sorry.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:43.330
Mom, I'm sorry.

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:48.070
Because of me, all your treasures broke.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.810
Do you want them back?

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:56.610
That's the price you paid for the cure.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:19:00.080
If you want them back, you'll 
have to do the opposite.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:06.570
Could you exchange her left arm for 
about ten outfits and ten jewels?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.680
What? Still not enough?

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:13.910
Then her right arm is next.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:16.630
If that's not enough,
you can give up both legs.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:18.340
And if that's still not enough—

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.850
Please stop!

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.540
Then what will you give up to get it back?

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:27.760
Will it be Koto's feelings again?

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:28.590
I get it!

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.090
I don't need anything besides Koto!

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.850
Mom.

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:40.920
The ambulance has arrived.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.860
Kuro, let's go.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.000
Right.

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:52.100
Doctor, that's the window.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:14.020
<i>Popular child actress Kashiwagi Koto-san was 
released from the hospital this morning.</i>

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:16.520
Agency comments: "She will
 be taking a short break."

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:16.520
Popular Child Actress Goes
 on Temporary Hiatus

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:19.520
<i>Her agency announced that she will be 
taking a break from the industry for a while.</i>

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:23.290
Kuro, thanks for saving us a spot.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:27.160
Doctor, these are all snacks.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:30.310
Do you expect us to view the 
flowers without actual lunches?

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:32.390
No, our lunches are—

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:33.920
Doctor, hello.

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:36.430
Thank you for waiting.

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.650
Hey, Koto. Congratulations on your release.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:41.910
Thank you.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.800
When did they become friends?

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:47.670
This looks delicious.

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.720
Thanks for the food!

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.930
It's been so long since I last cooked.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.760
I'm worried it won't taste good.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:02.940
Even if a dish uses the same recipe, ingredients, 
or seasoning, once you eat it, you'll know

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.870
how the cook felt when they made it.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:08.730
So I'm sure...

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.240
Thanks for the food.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.200
How is it, Koto?

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.940
It's good. It's delicious.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.460
That's odd.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:27.590
Am I still sick?

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.730
My tears are so salty.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:40.290
Dummy. That's what tears taste like.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:13.950
<b>Shiranui General Hospital</b>

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:23.230
Your penis certainly <i>is</i> a chikuwa fish cake.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:30.570
<i>Doctor, our next patient is coming 
to us from the nearby hospital.</i>

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:32.480
<i>Now that's one impressive—</i>

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:33.640
<i>It's a chikuwa.</i>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:37.020
<i>Dr. Ramune -Mysterious Disease Specialist-.</i>

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:39.330
<i>Episode 2, "The Chikuwa Penis."</i>

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Episode 2 
